# Connections: stat_connect

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`stat_connect()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/stat_connect.html), in the order the
page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly
cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a
list of what remains.

`stat_connect()` joins each observation to the next with a line of a chosen shape: `"hv"` goes
horizontally and then vertically, `"vh"` vertically and then horizontally, `"mid"` steps half-way
between the two `x` values, and `"linear"` goes straight. A shape of one's own is a matrix of
points on a path from (0, 0) to (1, 1), which is stretched to fit between each pair of
observations. Giggly has none of it yet.

## Steps

```r
ggplot(head(economics, 20), aes(date, unemploy)) +
  stat_connect(connection = "hv")
```

`head()` keeps the first 20 months of ggplot2's `economics` dataset, whose `unemploy` is the
number of unemployed in the US, in thousands.

Not in Giggly yet: `stat_connect()`.

## Connections of one's own

```r
# Setup custom connections
x <- seq(0, 1, length.out = 20)[-1]
smooth <- cbind(x, scales::rescale(1 / (1 + exp(-(x * 10 - 5)))))
zigzag <- cbind(c(0.4, 0.6, 1), c(0.75, 0.25, 1))

ggplot(head(economics, 10), aes(date, unemploy)) +
  geom_point() +
  stat_connect(aes(colour = "zigzag"), connection = zigzag) +
  stat_connect(aes(colour = "smooth"), connection = smooth)
```

`smooth` is an S-shaped curve and `zigzag` goes up, down and up again. Mapping `colour` to a
constant names each layer in the legend.

Not in Giggly yet: `stat_connect()` and its `connection` option given as a matrix.